Track 1: The Anchor Learns to Hover
- Story & Context: When midday vanished into an oily eclipse above Puerto Deseado, the boardwalk carnival collapsed into freezing twilight and the grease on Don Silvestro’s calliope burst into green flame. Instead of fleeing the smoke, three hundred dockworkers stood paralyzed as a five-meter contrabassoon blasted an impossible, weightless habanera across the receding mudflats. The bassoonist inhaled the smell of burning sugar and sea brine, dragging his reed across cold lips until the tide stalled mid-surge. Through the loudspeaker horn, a weeping contralto drifted over the frozen carousel, singing: "The tide forgets which shore it promised to drown."
