Track 2: Chamuyo en Pleamar
- Story & Context: Huddled in the bilge of a grounded schooner at Punta Mogotes during the three-minute total blackout, tango dancer Malena Ortiz confessed to smuggling celestial charts inside her hollowed bassoon bell. She pressed a salt-crusted silver peso under the customs magistrate's tongue to stop his stammering while her woodwind ensemble droned an airy, microtonal milonga that made the stagnant bilge water shiver. Every serrated kick of her heel against the hull shook another clandestine secret loose into the freezing gloom. Her voice drifted through the wooden ribs like sea mist, murmuring: "Forgive my ankles, Magistrate, they only obey the dark sun."
