Track 3: Did the Lighthouse Die of Cold?
- Story & Context: By the time the daylight snapped back over the salt flats of Cabo Raso, the entire eclipse carnival had evaporated into sea smoke, leaving only a circle of brine-frosted bassoons floating vertically like navigational beacons in the swell. Old harbor master Evaristo dredged a child's velvet mask and a drift-log scored with tango tabulations from the water, his lantern oil trembling to an ethereal low-register drone that the wooden reeds continued to breathe without human lungs. Legend holds that the orchestra stepped directly off the jetty during the moment of syzygy, their shoes weighted down with zinc sinkers. Scratched into the brass bell of the sunken contrabassoon was their final decree: "When the sky went blind, we danced out toward the deep water and forgot how to drown."
